## 8. REFERRAL ATTRIBUTION SYSTEM

Attribution Model: LAST CLICK ATTRIBUTION.

Cookie Duration: 30 days.

Important business rule:

When a customer clicks an Affiliate's referral link, that Affiliate receives referral attribution.

If the customer later clicks another Affiliate's referral link, the most recently clicked valid Affiliate receives the attribution.

Example:

- Customer clicks Affiliate A's link.
- Later, customer clicks Affiliate B's link.
- Affiliate B receives the referral credit.

### Website-Wide Attribution

After clicking a valid Affiliate referral link, the customer can purchase ANY eligible TeqqnoWorld product.

The commission must not be limited to the specific product included in the original referral link.

All eligible products purchased within the valid attribution window must be attributed to the last-click Affiliate.

### Cookie and Tracking

- Default cookie duration: 30 days.
- Admin configurable.
- Respect applicable cookie consent and privacy requirements.
- Use secure, HTTP-only, SameSite cookies where compatible with the architecture.
- Use server-side attribution validation.
- Support authenticated customer attribution across devices where identity can be reliably established and privacy requirements permit it.
- Do not promise cross-device tracking for unidentified visitors.
- Do not overwrite a newer valid attribution with an older one.
- Expired attribution must not generate commission.
- Maintain an auditable attribution history.

### Click Tracking

Record:
- Date.
- Time.
- Affiliate ID.
- Referral token.
- Landing Product/Page.
- Device.
- Browser.
- Traffic Source.
- Campaign information where available.
- IP-derived fraud signals only when legally permitted and necessary.

Avoid collecting unnecessary personal data.

### Self-Referral Prevention

Self-referrals must be blocked automatically.

If an Affiliate attempts to purchase through their own referral link:

- Do not award commission.
- Flag the event for fraud monitoring.
- Record the reason.
- Notify Admin where appropriate.

Use reliable authenticated customer identity checks.

Do not rely only on IP address because multiple legitimate users can share the same IP.

